  "description": "Deliver one epic of the approved roadmap (docs/phases.md steps 7 to 10). The epic case opens child cases in order, each once every earlier child ended passed: sdc.spec (the ESS specification, authored, reused or reconstructed, until the ESS gate passes), sdc.plan (the AEP stories), one sdc.story case per story (opened together), then sdc.release. No action is admissible before the roadmap is approved, and none after the specification stage before the ESS gate passes on the current specification revision. The case ends passed once the release case ended passed and the gate still passes, or abandoned on an explicit decision; when a child case ended other than passed it ends not_delivered (a child before the release) or not_released (the release), without a person.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "description": "the outcome of one child case, one record per child: passed or another outcome of the child's protocol, open while the child runs",
      "name": "case_outcome",
      "produced_by": []
    },
    {
      "description": "the ESS gate over a specification revision: `ess specify validate --strict-requires`, `ess specify compile`, `ess verify conform synthesize` with 0 refusals and no `UNMAPPED:` marker, run as one program; passed only when all four pass, failed otherwise",
